package scenes

const sceneDirectionPrompt = `ART DIRECTION AND VISIBLE ACTION:
Treat the brief as a storyboard, not a request for a generic title card. Establish a recognizable primary subject, a supporting environment and only the detail needed to tell this specific story. Specify a coherent palette, light, material/texture treatment, foreground/midground/background separation and typographic hierarchy. Richness means purposeful visual relationships, not more boxes, gradients, particles or unreadable copy. Respect an intentionally minimal user brief.

Build a legible reveal, a meaningful change/action, a settled reading/viewing hold and an intentional exit. Scale choreography to the actual duration; do not cram every beat into the first second. Keep the primary subject visible during the central hold and for most of the scene. Clamp entrance and exit progress separately: opacity = entrance * (1 - exit); never reuse an entrance progress as a fade-out or leave the whole scene at opacity:0. A CSS animation must use explicit pixel/percentage endpoints, a real nonzero duration and a stable fill state. Prefer frame-derived transforms/opacity. Set explicit root and layer dimensions, positioning and stacking order; do not let a full-frame background cover the artwork. Avoid clipped/offscreen subjects, zero-sized SVG viewBoxes/canvases, invisible dark-on-dark objects and entrance transforms that never settle. Test the mental frame at 0%, 20%, 50%, 80% and 100%, including a backward seek. Never solve a compiler/layout repair by deleting the imagery, disabling opacity, removing requested motion or replacing the scene with a heading.

When the request calls for depth, an orbit, a spatial mechanism, lighting, materials or moving meshes, use genuine SceneThree, including in auto mode when that is the best medium. A CSS-rotated rectangle or SVG pseudo-sphere does not satisfy a Three.js/3D request. Make the geometry substantial and relevant, size it to the camera frustum, aim camera.lookAt at the subject, set near/far safely, and use ambient/key/fill light for lit materials. Give the camera a purposeful path and derive each mesh/camera transform directly from frame time so reverse seeking works. Returning an empty setup, black canvas, stationary demo primitive or unused SceneThree import is not a completed spatial scene. The runtime example is an API starter, not artwork to copy unchanged. Do not invent loaders or libraries.

ON-SCREEN COPY POLICY:
Do not add AI-production labels, disclaimers, watermarks, technical job IDs or badges anywhere on screen. Forbidden automatic copy includes 'AI illustration', 'AI-generated', 'Generated with AI', 'Ilustrație AI', 'Generat cu AI' and 'Narațiune sintetică'. Scene titles, explanations, implementation notes and provenance metadata are not on-screen copy. Keep any explanation outside the component. Render only subject-relevant supplied copy/labels, and preserve a genuinely requested subject about artificial intelligence without adding a production notice. Do not bake such notices into supplied/generated artwork, CSS pseudo-elements, SVG, canvas or Three.js textures.`
